# Deny everything, then allow back only what the build actually needs.
#
# An allow-list rather than a deny-list on purpose: with a deny-list, every new
# file or directory added to the repo silently joins the build context, and the
# failure mode is leaking something (a .sql snapshot, credentials, notes) into
# an image layer. Here, anything new is excluded until explicitly permitted.
*

!package.json
!package-lock.json
!src/

# NO RE-EXCLUSIONS UNDER src/, DELIBERATELY. A re-exclusion covers only the
# shapes it names, so the first file that does not match the pattern ships
# without anyone noticing.
#
# The rule to keep: if it is under src/, it ships. Anything that must not ship
# goes outside src/ rather than getting a pattern here.

# THE ONE EXCEPTION to that, because it cannot be relocated: Finder writes
# .DS_Store into every directory it browses, so it turns up under src/ without
# anyone putting it there.
#
# It needs the `**/` to work. `*` matches a single path segment, so it never
# sees src/anything -- and `!src/` re-includes that whole subtree, nested junk
# included. Verified: with `*` and `!src/` alone, src/.DS_Store ships.
**/.DS_Store
